## Review: diff vs. issue #59

**Diff summary:** single-line change in `src/app/(home)/page.tsx`, swapping `items-center` → `items-stretch` on the wrapper `<div className="mt-24 flex flex-col ...">` around `<Cards>`.

**(a) Missing / partial requirements**

- Acceptance criterion: *"Verified visually via playwright-mcp, not just by reading class names"* — no evidence this was done. I attempted it myself: started `pnpm dev` (confirmed ready via server log — Next.js 16.3.1, `Ready in 2.3s`), then tried `mcp__playwright__browser_navigate` against `http://localhost:3000`, `http://172.17.0.3:3000`, and `http://host.docker.internal:3000`. All failed (`ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED`, timeout, `ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED`) — the playwright browser tool runs in a network-isolated sandbox that can't reach the bash-launched dev server in this environment. So this criterion is still unverified end-to-end; only static/DOM-logic verification was possible here.

**(b) Scope creep**

- None. `git diff origin/main` touches exactly one file, one line — precisely the fix suggested in the issue's "What to build" section ("drop `items-center` in favor of `items-stretch`"). No unrelated formatting, refactors, or extra class changes.

**(c) Requirements that look implemented but may be wrong**

- None found; the fix is logically sound on inspection:
  - `Cards` renders as a plain `<div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 @container">` (confirmed in `@fumadocs/base-ui/dist/components/card.js`), and `Card` carries `@max-lg:col-span-full` exactly as the issue describes.
  - `items-stretch` is flexbox's *default* `align-items` value for a column flex container — the original `items-center` was an explicit override causing shrink-to-fit sizing of the `Cards` grid, which collapsed the `@container` width. Restoring `items-stretch` lets the grid div fill the parent's inline size, so the container-query breakpoints (`@max-lg:col-span-full`) now evaluate against the real viewport-derived width at both mobile and desktop sizes.
  - Since `flex-direction: column`, `align-items` only affects the cross axis (width), not height — no unintended vertical stretching of the grid.
  - `HomeHero` (`/home/agent/workspace/src/app/_components/home-hero.tsx`) is a **sibling** rendered before the changed wrapper div, both nested in `<div className="relative">` — it is not a flex child of the modified container, so its own centering/spacing (`max-md:text-center`, `max-md:mx-auto` on its CTA row) is structurally unreachable by this change. "No regression to hero centering" is satisfied by construction, not just incidentally.

**Files referenced:** `/home/agent/workspace/src/app/(home)/page.tsx`, `/home/agent/workspace/src/app/_components/home-hero.tsx`, `node_modules/.pnpm/@fumadocs+base-ui@16.15.0.../dist/components/card.js`.Both review agents have reported back. Aggregating:

